# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
# ...but the bundled SlateDB native library is tracked
!lib/libslatedb_uniffi.so

# Local data directory created by the server
/yasdb-data/

# Maelstrom test store (results/logs) and stray built binaries
/store/
/maelstrom-adapter
/yasdb

# k6 load-test run artifacts (summaries + metric dumps)
/k6/results/

# Ad-hoc metric exports dropped in the repo root (Grafana/k6 downloads)
/result*.json
/results*.zip

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Live State UI bundle build tooling — ui/dist/live-state.bundle.js (the
# go:embed'd build output) is tracked; only node_modules is not.
/ui/node_modules/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
